    <div class="itdgl-faq-list" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/FAQPage">
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What channels generate the most patient leads for a Thane hair transplant clinic?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Google Search + Ads 25-30% (highest-intent 'hair transplant near me' + 'FUE cost' queries), Meta + Instagram + Reels 25-30%, YouTube + long-form ads 15-20%, GMB + local search 15-20%, WhatsApp CTWA + inside-sales 10-15%, medical-tourism campaigns for Tier 2/3 + international 10-20%, organic SEO 10-15%, referral 10-20%.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What CPQL for a Thane hair transplant clinic?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Rs 500-1,500 general hair-transplant inquiry, Rs 800-2,500 FUE/DHI-specific + graft-count-qualified, Rs 1,500-5,000 high-AOV bespoke consultation. Lead-to-consultation 15-30%. Cost per booked consultation Rs 3,000-15,000. Consultation-to-treatment 20-40%. Effective cost per acquired patient Rs 15,000-60,000. Justified by AOV Rs 60K-4L per procedure + Rs 20K-1.2L maintenance LTV.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How does WhatsApp + inside-sales flow work for Thane hair transplant lead conversion?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">High-touch inside-sales for high-AOV. WhatsApp CTWA → Interakt/AiSensy auto-reply → chatbot qualification → dedicated inside-sales rep human handoff within 3 min business hours. Inside-sales flow: hair-loss assessment + graft-count estimate + video-consultation booking + facility tour link + surgeon-credentials PDF + procedure-cost breakdown + travel/stay coordination (medical-tourism) + booking confirmation + pre-op prep + post-op care + 6-12 month growth documentation follow-up. Conversion 20-40% inside-sales-qualified to consultation booking. Marathi + Hindi + English + Gujarati + English + Hindi native templates. Medical-tourism-specific dedicated rep.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What lead qualification for hair transplant?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">BANT + fit + hair-loss stage (Norwood scale) + graft-count estimate + budget tier (Rs 60K-2L, Rs 2-5L, Rs 5L+) + timeline (immediate/6mo/exploring) + location (local vs medical-tourism). MQL score ≥ 50 (higher threshold). SQL ≥ 70 or specific procedure intent + budget indicator. CRM + Klaviyo + custom high-AOV tracking.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How do we track hair transplant patient lead flow end-to-end?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">CRM + multi-touch attribution over 90-180 day consideration cycle + offline conversion upload (phone/inside-sales/consultation close — 30-50% attribution loss without) + medical-tourism catchment split + procedure-revenue attribution.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How much monthly lead flow for a Thane hair transplant clinic?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Solo (Rs 10-30 lakh): 40-150 inquiries → 15-50 video-consultations → 8-25 in-person → 3-12 procedures. 2-3 surgeon (Rs 30 lakh-1.5 crore): 150-400 → 50-150 → 25-80 → 12-40 procedures. Multi-location/destination: 400+ → 150+ → 80+ → 40+ procedures.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How do landing pages + content-led lead-gen work for hair transplant?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Landing pages per procedure (Thane-specific: FUE Cost Thane, Hair Transplant Thane) + graft-count calculator interactive tool + facility virtual tour + surgeon credentials + video testimonials + before-after library + booking CTA + WhatsApp inside-sales button. Medical-tourism landing pages for Tier 2/3 + international catchment. Conversion 3-8% for well-executed.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What compliance issues for hair transplant lead-gen?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Same base + surgical + medical-tourism-specific: no guaranteed graft-yield + no aggressive discount + no comparative claims + surgeon credentials verifiable + facility norms + medical-tourism both-jurisdiction compliance.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How do we handle patient referrals for a Thane hair transplant clinic?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">6/12/18/24-month post-procedure WhatsApp asks for review + referral. Referral incentive structured (ethics-compliant). Referral LTV 4-6x paid lead LTV — highest of three clinic types because procedure is transformative + patient loyalty extreme.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What are common lead-gen mistakes for Thane hair transplant clinics?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">(1) No WhatsApp inside-sales flow (misses 30-50% high-AOV close). (2) Missing offline conversion upload. (3) Weak multi-touch attribution. (4) Under-invested video creative. (5) Same creative + audience local vs medical-tourism. (6) No graft-count calculator. (7) English-only in Thane. (8) Aggressive discount marketing. (9) Weak surgeon-credibility + facility landing pages. (10) No YouTube long-form ads.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What monthly reporting for hair transplant lead-gen?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Weekly: CPL + cost per video-consultation + in-person consultation + procedure booking + inside-sales conversion + WhatsApp response rate + medical-tourism catchment mix. Monthly QBR: full P&amp;L + procedure revenue attribution + graft-count-weighted + medical-tourism split + cohort LTV. Quarterly business review + long-cycle content library audit.</div>
